# Everything the image does not need, kept out of the build context.
#
# This is not only about speed. The context is uploaded to the daemon and any of it can end up in
# a layer, so `.env`, user secrets, and local database state are excluded for the same reason they
# are gitignored: a file that never enters the context cannot leak from an image.

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/bin/
**/obj/
artifacts/
TestResults/
*.binlog

# ── Version control and IDE state ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Note what is NOT excluded: .editorconfig. It carries analyzer severities the build depends on
# (see the Dockerfile's restore stage), so excluding it would make the image compile under
# different rules than CI — a failure that looks like a random analyzer error.
**/.git/
**/.gitignore
**/.github/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# ── Tests ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Excluded deliberately, and the Dockerfile depends on it: because the test projects are absent,
# the image restores the *host project* rather than GymOS.Backend.slnx (which references them).
# Tests run in CI against the source, never inside the runtime image.
tests/

# ── Documentation and infrastructure definitions ─────────────────────────────────
docs/
*.md
docker-compose*.yml
docker/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Secrets and local state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/*.pfx
**/appsettings.*.Local.json
.docker-data/

# ── Frontend (separate repository; here only if someone nests one) ──────────────
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
